__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.venv/

# Microscope images acquired alongside the spectra: kept locally, not in git
# (see README "Input data"). Raw spectra (input/*.csv/.txt) and params/*.xlsx
# ARE tracked — the input spectra are the measured source data and are NOT
# reproducible, so they stay in the repo.
input/**/*.czi
input/**/*.bmp
input/**/*.png
# Generated RESULTS in output/ (figures, CSVs, JSON) are reproducible from the
# input spectra + configs, so they are not tracked. The SCRIPTS in output/ are:
# they are the figure- and table-generation layer on top of the root pipeline,
# and they are what the paper's "deposited in repo [49]" claim actually points
# to. Ignoring them would have left that claim backed by nothing but the core
# pipeline, with every published figure and SM table unreproducible.
# Archive a canonical results set with the tagged release if a frozen, citable
# copy of the numbers is also required (see paper-tracker.md G).
# NB `output/*` not `output/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so the directory itself must not be the ignored entry.
output/*
!output/*.py
*.docx
Paper WIP Draft.docx
paper-tracker.md
Chemical Disorder Final.xlsx
Cross Spectrum Ratios original.xlsx
# Paper-working data (this folder was renamed from "Stress Mapping/"): stress-map
